                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game isn't TERRIBLE, but it's not great either.\n-AI is pretty basic, they can't open doors, so they'll just bang into/shoot it until you open it, making it pretty hard to avoid damage. \n-You can only carry 1 health item, but you can pick up multiple, which just deletes your previous one. \n-I got stuck and couldn't figure out what to do after 10 minutes.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1488687173,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1488687173,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 12,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.6104356050491333,
                        "comment_count": 0,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Hi KarmaChicken,\n\nSorry you didn't enjoy Biotoxin. As for your complaints, the early AI is mainly the infected which are designed to be basic. Once you encounter more advanced human AI towards the middle-end of the game, they can open doors and set up ambushes.\nWith higher calibre weapons, you can also shoot through thinner objects such as doors.\nWhich part of the game couldn't you get through? Perhaps I could help.\n\nThanks,\nFivesyounger",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1488706936,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": true
                    }
